Relevant columns and their potential usages  
• "project_short_name": filter rows belonging only to the TCGA‑BRCA project.  
• "sample_type_name": pick “Solid Tissue Normal” rows; also useful for counting or verifying other sample‑type categories.  
• "gene_type": restrict to “protein_coding” genetic elements.  
• "HTSeq__FPKM_UQ": the un‑stranded upper‑quartile‑normalized FPKM value whose variance we ultimately want to examine.  
• "gene_name" / "Ensembl_gene_id": group‑by keys when aggregating expression values per gene.  
• "case_barcode": identify unique cases; can be paired with a sub‑query to be sure we keep only BRCA cases that have ≥1 “Solid Tissue Normal” sample.  
• "sample_barcode", "aliquot_barcode": optional granular identifiers that may be handy when drilling down into repeated measures.  

Typical conditions you may combine  
• WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA‑BRCA'  
• AND   "sample_type_name" = 'Solid Tissue Normal'  
• AND   "gene_type" = 'protein_coding'  
• HAVING COUNT(*) ≥ 2                    -- when computing variance you need at least two observations per gene  
• AND "case_barcode" IN ( …sub‑query keeping only cases that include Solid Tissue Normal … )  

Below are ten exploratory Snowflake SQL queries (simple → complex) that help inspect the data and pave the way toward the final analysis.  
All column names are enclosed in double quotes and each query is limited to 20 rows.

```sql
-- 1) Description: List distinct projects available in the table (sanity‑check BRCA exists)
SELECT DISTINCT "project_short_name"
FROM TCGA.TCGA_VERSIONED.RNASEQ_HG38_GDC_R28
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2) Description: Show distinct sample‑type names that appear in TCGA‑BRCA
SELECT DISTINCT "sample_type_name"
FROM TCGA.TCGA_VERSIONED.RNASEQ_HG38_GDC_R28
WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3) Description: Count how many rows fall into each sample type for TCGA‑BRCA
SELECT "sample_type_name",
       COUNT(*) AS "row_cnt"
FROM TCGA.TCGA_VERSIONED.RNASEQ_HG38_GDC_R28
WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
GROUP BY "sample_type_name"
ORDER BY "row_cnt" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4) Description: Preview 20 Solid Tissue Normal rows (all genes, any gene_type)
SELECT "case_barcode",
       "sample_barcode",
       "gene_name",
       "gene_type",
       "HTSeq__FPKM_UQ"
FROM TCGA.TCGA_VERSIONED.RNASEQ_HG38_GDC_R28
WHERE "project_short_name"  = 'TCGA-BRCA'
  AND "sample_type_name"    = 'Solid Tissue Normal'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5) Description: Check which gene_type values appear inside Solid Tissue Normal for TCGA‑BRCA
SELECT DISTINCT "gene_type"
FROM TCGA.TCGA_VERSIONED.RNASEQ_HG38_GDC_R28
WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
  AND "sample_type_name"   = 'Solid Tissue Normal'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6) Description: Preview protein‑coding genes only, Solid Tissue Normal samples
SELECT "gene_name",
       "Ensembl_gene_id",
       "HTSeq__FPKM_UQ"
FROM TCGA.TCGA_VERSIONED.RNASEQ_HG38_GDC_R28
WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
  AND "sample_type_name"   = 'Solid Tissue Normal'
  AND "gene_type"          = 'protein_coding'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7) Description: Count how many Solid Tissue Normal measurements exist per protein‑coding gene
SELECT "gene_name",
       COUNT(*) AS "num_samples"
FROM TCGA.TCGA_VERSIONED.RNASEQ_HG38_GDC_R28
WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
  AND "sample_type_name"   = 'Solid Tissue Normal'
  AND "gene_type"          = 'protein_coding'
GROUP BY "gene_name"
ORDER BY "num_samples" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8) Description: Identify BRCA cases (case_barcodes) that contain at least one Solid Tissue Normal sample
SELECT DISTINCT "case_barcode"
FROM TCGA.TCGA_VERSIONED.RNASEQ_HG38_GDC_R28
WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
  AND "sample_type_name"   = 'Solid Tissue Normal'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9) Description: For those cases, fetch protein‑coding Solid Tissue Normal expression values
SELECT t."case_barcode",
       t."sample_barcode",
       t."gene_name",
       t."HTSeq__FPKM_UQ"
FROM   TCGA.TCGA_VERSIONED.RNASEQ_HG38_GDC_R28 t
WHERE  t."project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
  AND  t."gene_type"          = 'protein_coding'
  AND  t."sample_type_name"   = 'Solid Tissue Normal'
  AND  t."case_barcode" IN (
        SELECT DISTINCT "case_barcode"
        FROM TCGA.TCGA_VERSIONED.RNASEQ_HG38_GDC_R28
        WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
          AND "sample_type_name"   = 'Solid Tissue Normal'
       )
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--10) Description: Compute variance of FPKM‑UQ per protein‑coding gene (need ≥2 samples); 
--                results ordered by descending variance (top genes). 
--                Limited to 20 rows to preview, not the final 5.
SELECT "gene_name",
       VAR_SAMP("HTSeq__FPKM_UQ") AS "fpkm_uq_variance",
       COUNT(*)                   AS "num_samples"
FROM TCGA.TCGA_VERSIONED.RNASEQ_HG38_GDC_R28
WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
  AND "sample_type_name"   = 'Solid Tissue Normal'
  AND "gene_type"          = 'protein_coding'
GROUP BY "gene_name"
HAVING COUNT(*) >= 2
ORDER BY "fpkm_uq_variance" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

These queries incrementally surface the column content and aggregation logic you would use to pinpoint the five protein‑coding genes with the greatest expression variance in TCGA‑BRCA Solid Tissue Normal samples.
